{
  "name": "material-point",
  "dimension": "3D",
  "full_name": "Material Point FISH Intrinsics",
  "description": "Pointer-based FISH access to material points -- the MPM carriers of mass, stress and history. This is the ONLY scripted access to material points: they have no Python binding. MPoint3D is 3D.",
  "notes": [
    "Material points are not exposed to the Python API. itasca.* reports a count of zero after 'mpoint import from-zones' even though the points exist -- use these intrinsics.",
    "Iterate with 'loop foreach local mp mpoint.list' rather than assuming contiguous IDs.",
    "An intrinsic whose signature ends in ':= <type>' can be assigned to, not just read (for example mpoint.vel(mp) = vector(0,0,0)).",
    "Properties are constitutive-model-specific: mpoint.prop(mp,'young') works only if the assigned model has that property. See references/constitutive-models."
  ],
  "intrinsic_count": 61,
  "intrinsic_families": [
    {
      "family": "iteration & identity",
      "intrinsics": [
        {
          "name": "mpoint.list",
          "signature": "mpmpoint_list_pnt = mpoint.list()"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.num",
          "signature": "int = mpoint.num()"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.maxid",
          "signature": "int = mpoint.maxid()"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.find",
          "signature": "MPM_POINT_pnt = mpoint.find(int)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.id",
          "signature": "int := mpoint.id(mpm_point_pnt)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.typeid",
          "signature": "int = mpoint.typeid()"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.near",
          "signature": "MPM_POINT_pnt = mpoint.near(vec3+,<flt>)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.containing",
          "signature": "MPM_POINT_pnt = mpoint.containing(vec3+,<index>)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.inbox",
          "signature": "list = mpoint.inbox(vec3+,vec3+,<bool>)"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "mpoint.containing(pos) finds the point occupying a position, mpoint.near(pos,<radius>) the closest one, and mpoint.inbox(lo,hi) every point in a box."
      ]
    },
    {
      "family": "creation & deletion",
      "intrinsics": [
        {
          "name": "mpoint.create",
          "signature": "mpm_point_pnt := mpoint.create(flt,vec3+,<int>)"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.delete",
          "signature": "bool := mpoint.delete(mpm_point_pnt)"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "FISH can build and destroy material points directly -- mpoint.create(volume,position) -- which is the scripted alternative to 'mpoint create' / 'mpoint generate'."
      ]
    },
    {
      "family": "geometry & motion",
      "intrinsics": [
        {
          "name": "mpoint.pos",
          "signature": "vec3/flt := mpoint.pos(mpm_point_pnt,<int>) := vec3/flt"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.pos.x",
          "signature": "flt := mpoint.pos.x(mpm_point_pnt) := flt"
        },
        {
          "name": "mpoint.pos.y",
          "signature": "flt := mpoint.pos.y(mpm_point_pnt) := flt"
        },
